.env
.env.local
# ⚠️ Every other variant too — a hand-made `.env.bak.20260816` holding a
# production `DATABASE_URL` is the same secret in a file nobody thought to
# ignore, and `railway up` uploads the WORKING TREE. Neither of the two lines
# above matched one. `.env.example` is committed and stays committed.
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
frames/
*.sqlite
.DS_Store

# Working plans — documents written to be executed against this repo and spent
# once they were. Untracked 2026-08-20, before this went public. They are
# instructions to an agent rather than documentation of the result: what a plan
# proposed and what actually shipped diverge, and a reader cannot tell which
# from the file. **The result is what `MEASUREMENTS.md` and the CLAUDE.md files
# are for**, and the two that were here are in the archived pre-public history.
docs/plan-*.md

# the UI: source lives in web/src, everything below is generated
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
# the staged export api.py serves at "/". Build output, never source —
# `cd web && npm run prod:local` puts it here.
waterline/web/

# Source art for the rat: a 20MB rigged FBX and 23MB of 4K PBR maps.
# What ships is web/public/rat/ — four stills (37KB) and four animated loops
# (760KB), all baked offline. The model is licensed to be rendered, not
# redistributed, and 44MB of binaries is a permanent history cost on a repo
# whose basemap is 27KB of committed numbers.
# Regenerate with `web/scripts/rat-bake.py` (bake+webp, then loop+loopwebp).
# (`frames/` above already covers assets/black-rat/frames/ at any depth —
#  which is where the 84 loop renders and the 63MB .blend cache land.)
assets/black-rat/

# Candidates for the OTHER rat — the graffiti one on the card backs. Four 1024²
# diffusion outputs and their keyed previews, ~6.5MB, from
# `web/scripts/rat-graffiti.py generate`. Only the picked one ships, as
# web/public/rat/rat-graffiti.webp (86KB), and that IS committed. Same trade as
# the black-rat source above: keep the input reproducible from a script, keep
# the megabytes out of history.
web/scripts/.rat-graffiti/

# The landing and sign-in photographs at camera resolution — seven 5504×3072
# JPEGs, 79MB. What ships is web/public/photoz/*.webp, seven files at 2200px
# and 2.0MB the set, and those ARE committed. Same trade as the two above:
# keep the source on disk, keep the megabytes out of history.
#
#   cd web/public/photoz
#   for f in ../../photoz-src/*.jpg; do
#     cwebp -q 72 -resize 2200 0 -m 6 -metadata none "$f" \
#       -o "$(basename "${f%.jpg}").webp"
#   done
web/photoz-src/

# Screens the claude.ai/design agent built, downloaded back here as single-file
# bundles — ~1.3MB each, inlined CSS and fonts, and the browser numbers the
# duplicates. Same trade as the three above: keep the megabytes out of history.
#
# ⚠️ These are EVIDENCE and the evidence is worth reading before it is deleted.
# `Estuary-Dashboard-2A` is where the two live cascade defects were found — the
# thirteen tokens frozen by `var()` at `:root`, and the unlayered `*` from
# `@neondatabase/auth` outranking every border-colour utility in the app. `tsc`,
# `vitest` and `next build` were all green through both. What SURVIVES a delete
# is the write-up: the root CLAUDE.md's design-system section, the
# `:root, [data-palette]` block in globals.css, and the split Tailwind import.
Estuary-Dashboard-*.html


# The two standalone mockups `/` and `/about` were built from, 2026-08-16 —
# single-file bundles from the same design surface, ~1.9MB the pair, with the
# real HTML inside a `__bundler/template` JSON payload rather than in the file.
#
# ⚠️ Same trade as the entry above, and the same caveat: these are the SOURCE of
# what shipped. What survives a delete is the code plus the accounting — the
# landing page's four conditions in `landing-sections.tsx`, and the four rules
# `/about` lost, listed in `about-sections.tsx` and `web/src/app/CLAUDE.md`.
#
# To read one back: `sed -n '384p' <file> | python3 -c \
#   "import sys,json; sys.stdout.write(json.loads(sys.stdin.read()))"`
fluud-*-standalone.html
